// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'executions'. Valid alternatives: ['query', 'mapping', 'runtime']
//
// `executions['key']: { ... }` is the Multi execution's keyed-parameter form. A Single
// execution has no such arm -- it takes query, mapping and runtime, flat.
//
// Paired with neg-service-single-body-in-multi.pure. The two execution flavours share the
// `execution:` keyword and differ only in the word that follows, which is exactly the kind
// of distinction a rewritten parser collapses into one permissive body rule.
###Service
Service fixture::neg::SingleWithExecutions
{
   pattern: '/fixture/neg/singlewithexecutions';
   documentation: 'Multi-only executions[...] inside a Single execution';
   execution: Single
   {
      executions['UAT']:
      {
         mapping: fixture::neg::Mapping;
         runtime: fixture::neg::Runtime;
      }
   }
}
